What Distinguishes This From Standard Watchlist Apps
1. Meaningful Change Detection
Most apps show absolute numbers. MarketPulse detects relative changes.

Not: "NVDA +2%"
Yes: "NVDA +2% while tech sector +0.5% (outperforming)"
2. Peer Context Automatic
Users don't manually compare. The system does it.

Fetches peer group prices
Calculates peer averages
Compares automatically
Surfaces the insight
3. Attention Budget
Respects that users can't act on 20 notifications.

Show top 3
Show top 5
Show top 10
Show all
4. Correlation Detection
When holdings move together, tells the user.

"Tech holdings are 85% correlated"
"Your picks are moving as a group; diversification isn't helping"
5. Data Freshness Transparency
Doesn't hide staleness. Shows it.

Live: Fresh data (< 1 minute old)
Delayed: Older than ideal (1-5 minutes)
Stale: Very old (> 5 minutes)
Unavailable: Fetch failed
6. Graceful Degradation
API fails? System still works.

Falls back to demo data
Falls back to last known snapshot
No crashes, no blank screens
